Date:   Thu Oct 15 16:03:40 2026 +0800

    fix(reasoning): resolve the gateway key group inside the dotenv reload
    
    An owner profile .env that replaces the canonical Gateway key spelling
    with an alias-only API_SERVER_KEY used to leave the launcher's old
    canonical value beside it in os.environ and in the refreshed deployment
    snapshot. The readers prefer the canonical name, so the reload served
    the stale launcher credential instead of the owner's explicit choice,
    and sparse named profiles inheriting the snapshot sent the wrong key.
    
    The canonical and legacy names are one precedence group in the reload
    layer too: resolve the reloaded file's own choice (canonical preferred
    within the file), then mirror it onto both spellings for os.environ and
    for the deployment snapshot. Sparse fallback and removed-key
    restoration are unchanged.
    
    Verified: new boundary test RED before the change, GREEN after;
    boundary 48 passed, 1 skipped; touched-area battery 292 passed,
    8 skipped; ruff diff gate clean; git diff --check clean.

