<a href="#"><img alt="P1" src="https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9" align="top"></a> **Profile key references resolve incorrectly**

A named profile with `model.api_key: ${LM_API_KEY}` and its own `LM_API_KEY` now captures the process key, or the unresolved literal when the process has no key. The read-only scope binds the profile's values only to the thread, but `get_config_snapshot()` copies a cache whose refresh explicitly expands against the process environment.

The LM Studio key reader returns that config value before checking the profile's environment. Both Gateway and runner probes can therefore use the wrong key and lose the model's supported reasoning levels. Capture and expand the profile's raw config under the read-only scope without changing `os.environ`.

**Knowledge Base Used:** [Configuration and integrations](https://app.greptile.com/hermes-webui/-/custom-context/knowledge-base/nesquena/hermes-webui/-/docs/configuration-and-integrations.md)
