<a href="#"><img alt="P1" src="https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9" align="top"></a> **Priority tier still races**

Moving the cache refresh before the scoped return does not fully fix provider inference. After `get_config_snapshot()` releases its lock, another profile can replace the shared cache before `_main_model_request_overrides()` calls `resolve_model_provider()` without the snapshot. When the provider is omitted, as in the new test, this can still drop the saved `service_tier: priority` or apply it to the wrong provider.

Pass the captured `config_data` into provider inference instead of relying on the shared cache being unchanged.

