If an operator replaces an owner-profile canonical key with an alias-only `API_SERVER_KEY`, this reload restores the launcher's old `HERMES_WEBUI_GATEWAY_API_KEY`. The snapshot keeps both names, and `_gateway_api_key()` chooses the old canonical key. Named profiles that inherit these defaults then send the wrong key and can fail authentication.

Resolve the owner's key choice before applying launcher fallbacks, both in the snapshot and in `os.environ`.
