<li><code class="notranslate">api/profiles.py:1819-1827</code>: the reload mirror promotes the dotenv <code class="notranslate">API_SERVER_KEY</code> over an explicit launcher <code class="notranslate">HERMES_WEBUI_GATEWAY_API_KEY</code>. Setup: the launcher exports <code class="notranslate">HERMES_WEBUI_GATEWAY_BASE_URL</code> + <code class="notranslate">HERMES_WEBUI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=launcher-key</code>, and the root <code class="notranslate">~/.hermes/.env</code> holds <code class="notranslate">API_SERVER_KEY=local-key</code>, the normal Agent install. After <code class="notranslate">_reload_dotenv</code>, <code class="notranslate">os.environ["HERMES_WEBUI_GATEWAY_API_KEY"]</code> and the deployment snapshot both hold <code class="notranslate">local-key</code>. On master it stays <code class="notranslate">launcher-key</code>. Codex: HTTP 200 on master, <strong>401 on this head</strong> for default and sparse named profiles, at startup and after reload.</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">api/gateway_chat.py:249-266</code> (<code class="notranslate">_gateway_request_environ</code>): the profile overlay lets a profile's <code class="notranslate">API_SERVER_KEY</code> replace the launcher credential on the <strong>shared</strong> URL. The Agent clones the root <code class="notranslate">.env</code> into new profiles, so a cloned profile sends its own copied key and gets 401 even with item 1 removed. Master builds the request env from the process env minus every key a profile <code class="notranslate">.env</code> loaded (<code class="notranslate">api/gateway_chat.py:1726</code> on master), so the launcher key wins there.</li>
