commit aac413d65b257819b81cc35b9bd2dc80c8782336
Author: pxxD1998 <214340659+pxxD1998@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 15 13:10:07 2026 +0800

    fix(reasoning): refresh the deployment snapshot and the scoped config cache
    
    Re-gate of ccc03cc1f9de: both findings reproduced, both fixed.
    
    - _reload_dotenv() now re-captures gateway_chat's launcher-owned Gateway
      snapshot (replacing values, dropping removed keys) whenever the process
      profile's dotenv is permanently reloaded, so after an onboarding apply or
      a process-wide switch a sparse named profile inherits the new endpoint,
      key and runs flag instead of the import-time values. The replacement is a
      single atomic rebind; named-profile overlays are unchanged, and temporary
      worker-environment mirrors never rewrite the snapshot.
    - get_config_snapshot() runs the shared-cache path/mtime refresh before the
      scoped-profile early return, so module-level cfg readers reached from the
      same scope (resolve_model_provider, alias resolution) see the request's
      own profile; the inferred-provider service_tier: priority case no longer
      drops to {}.
    
    Tests pin the runtime dotenv reload (new key, removed-key dropping), the
    scoped cache refresh (inferred-provider service_tier) and the
    mirror-exclusion boundary.

