11:> Automated coverage: ~11,500 tests collected via `./scripts/test.sh tests/ --collect-only -q`. Tests run on every PR via GitHub Actions on Python 3.11, 3.12, and 3.13 (3 parallel shards each), alongside a ruff lint gate, a headless browser smoke test, and a Docker smoke test. The suite covers the bootstrap/static wizard, real provider config persistence (`config.yaml` + `.env`), the `/api/onboarding/*` backend, the onboarding skip/existing-config guard, CSS regression coverage for thinking/tool card animation, streaming session persistence, mobile layout breakpoints, locale parity across 14 languages, and hundreds of issue/PR-pinned regression tests.
157:## Python lint gate (ruff) — forward-looking, new-code-only
159:The Python twin of the ESLint runtime guard. A curated `ruff` ruleset
160:(`[tool.ruff]` in `pyproject.toml`) catches latent-bug shapes — unused imports
169:change adds or modifies** (`scripts/ruff_lint.py --diff`), which keeps new code
174:# one-time dev setup (ruff is a dev-only tool):
175:pip install ruff            # or: uv tool install ruff / uvx ruff ...
177:python3 scripts/ruff_lint.py --diff origin/master
179:python3 scripts/ruff_lint.py --all
182:`tests/test_ruff_forward_lint.py` holds the **whole tree** free of E9 (real
184:when ruff is present and **skips gracefully** when it isn't — so environments
185:without ruff aren't blocked, while CI (which installs ruff) enforces it. The

