/bin/bash -lc "git add api/gateway_chat.py api/profiles.py tests/test_gateway_runs_model_options_boundary.py && git commit -F - <<'MSG'
fix(reasoning): keep the launcher gateway key over a profile alias

The reload mirror promoted a dotenv API_SERVER_KEY over an explicit launcher
HERMES_WEBUI_GATEWAY_API_KEY, in os.environ and in the refreshed deployment
snapshot. Readers prefer the canonical name, so the default profile and sparse
named profiles sent the Agent's own key to the shared Gateway and were
rejected with 401. The request overlay had the same shape for a cloned
profile: its copied .env alias replaced the launcher credential.

Resolve the canonical/legacy key group in the documented order - profile
canonical, launcher canonical, profile alias, shared fallback - before
normalizing the two spellings, and only mirror an alias onto the canonical
name at reload when no launcher canonical exists. An explicit dotenv canonical
still replaces the launcher value.

Verified: new boundary tests RED before the change (reload mirror, request
overlay, and the Authorization header the real worker puts on the wire for the
default, sparse named and cloned named profile), GREEN after; boundary 52
passed, 1 skipped; boundary plus the #1879 liveness, #716 heartbeat and #5139
approval-offline tests 87 passed, 1 skipped; gateway/profile battery 975
passed, 74 skipped; ruff diff gate unchanged (6 pre-existing findings, none in
the touched files); git diff --check clean.
